13 years ago we started Māoriland with no money, no cinema, no hotels but a dream to bring Indigenous filmmakers and audiences together in our home town - Ōtaki. 

Today the Māoriland Film Festival welcomes audiences and filmmakers in their thousands from all over the world. 
We’re also making and reversioning films, training rangatahi, developing feature films, and showcasing artists year round from the @maorilandhub and @toimatarau.

We’re proud to be part of the @indigenous.cinema.alliance and to be part of a creative community of storytellers that reaches all around the world. 

