If you’ve checked out the @darwin.waterfront or @darwinbotanicgardens you might have seen works of art by these amazing artists - with three more starting next week! 

@liv_jelli101 is a Garramilla based artist, born & raised in country Victoria. Liv first began spray painting through the Babes Paint space in Darwin, a safe and welcoming spray painting space for women & LGBTQIA+ peeps founded by the incredible Hannah Illingsworth. As a social worker in the youth space Liv has always been passionate about social justice. She hopes to make political & social issues fun and accessible by combining them with pop culture moments in paint. 

@michelle_newton_art is an acrylic artist based in Darwin, known for her fun, bold and colourful work. A selftaught creative, she has built her practice through observation, curiosity and a love of capturing life on canvas. Her style is vibrant and expressive, inspired by her travels and the beauty she finds in everyday moments. Her art practice focuses on mark making, both gestural marks and the marks our lives leave on the people and world around us.

@aaronmooreart Aaron studied at the National Art School in Sydney and gained his higher education from the University of Oxford, UK, and the University of New South Wales’ Art and Design, Australia, where he earned masters degrees in Refugee Studies (MSc) and Fine Arts (MRes) respectively. Aaron has exhibited in multiple group and solo shows, recently winning the Walter Bennett Art Award, the Portrait of a Senior Territorian (2025), and the Katherine Art Award Packing Prize (2025). 

